What was your primary contribution to the project?

I focused primarily on the hardware assembly and circuit wiring, setting up the breadboard layout, positioning the LED and current-limiting resistor, and connecting the signal and ground lines to the Raspberry Pi.

What was the most challenging technical problem your team encountered?

The biggest challenge was handling unexpected user input types and ensuring robust input validation so the program wouldn't crash if non-numeric characters were entered.

How did your team use testing or debugging to solve a problem?

We performed iterative terminal tests with both valid temperature numbers and invalid inputs, verifying that our exception handling worked smoothly and that data logged correctly to the text file.

Which skills from CSE 1106 were most useful?

Defensive programming, error handling (try-except structures), and systematic requirements testing principles were the most helpful.

What would you improve if you had more time?

If we had more time, we would develop a simple graphical user interface (GUI) or web dashboard to make the monitoring interface more visual and user-friendly.
